{"rank": 68, "article": "Charlie Kirk", "revid": 1319750448, "parentid": 1319746898, "user": "Mikewem", "timestamp": "2025-10-31T17:07:25Z", "comment": "Undid revision [[Special:Diff/1319746898|1319746898]] by [[Special:Contributions/Dark Dreaming|Dark Dreaming]] ([[User talk:Dark Dreaming|talk]])We do say assassinated. In the 2nd sentence. There’s no benefit from using the word twice in the lead", "tags": ["mw-undo", "mobile edit", "mobile web edit", "advanced mobile edit", "wikieditor"], "size": 216083}
{"rank": 68, "article": "Charlie Kirk", "revid": 1319746898, "parentid": 1319741850, "user": "Dark Dreaming", "timestamp": "2025-10-31T16:42:56Z", "comment": "Undid revision [[Special:Diff/1319741850|1319741850]] by [[Special:Contributions/Captain Cornwall|Captain Cornwall]] ([[User talk:Captain Cornwall|talk]]) the talk page has agreed to use assassination (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Charlie_Kirk#Extended-confirmed-protected_edit_request_on_15_October_2025). if you dont think the word should be hyperlinked, then you can remove that - but dont change the wording", "tags": ["mw-undo", "mw-reverted", "wikieditor"], "size": 216098}
{"rank": 68, "article": "Charlie Kirk", "revid": 1319741850, "parentid": 1319634693, "user": "Captain Cornwall", "timestamp": "2025-10-31T16:01:32Z", "comment": "Avoiding overlinking", "tags": ["mobile edit", "mobile web edit", "advanced mobile edit", "mw-reverted"], "size": 216083}
{"rank": 68, "article": "Charlie Kirk", "revid": 1319634693, "parentid": 1319630047, "user": "Mikewem", "timestamp": "2025-10-31T00:13:59Z", "comment": "Declarations? After this would be statements. If it must be “statements”, I would request that we go with “public statements”. Again, it’s not notably controversial that he said them, it’s notably controversial that he said them on his show (for the public)", "tags": ["mobile edit", "mobile web edit", "advanced mobile edit"], "size": 216098}
{"rank": 68, "article": "Charlie Kirk", "revid": 1319630047, "parentid": 1319628263, "user": "Newimpartial", "timestamp": "2025-10-30T23:37:12Z", "comment": "Undid revision [[Special:Diff/1319628263|1319628263]] by [[Special:Contributions/Mikewem|Mikewem]] ([[User talk:Mikewem|talk]]) \"Assertions\" seems less neutral to me than \"views\", though neither seems ideal.", "tags": ["mw-undo", "mobile edit", "mobile app edit", "android app edit", "advanced mobile edit", "app-undo"], "size": 216091}
{"rank": 68, "article": "Charlie Kirk", "revid": 1319628263, "parentid": 1319624070, "user": "Mikewem", "timestamp": "2025-10-30T23:20:21Z", "comment": "I support this format as npov. I struggled to find the word that these things are. I landed on “assertions”. The idea is it’s not notably controversial that he inwardly held these views, it’s controversial that he expounded or “asserted” them.", "tags": ["mobile edit", "mobile web edit", "advanced mobile edit", "mw-reverted"], "size": 216096}
{"rank": 68, "article": "Charlie Kirk", "revid": 1319624070, "parentid": 1319623896, "user": "Tryptofish", "timestamp": "2025-10-30T22:45:18Z", "comment": "/* top */ further fix", "tags": ["wikieditor"], "size": 216091}
{"rank": 68, "article": "Charlie Kirk", "revid": 1319623896, "parentid": 1319569490, "user": "Tryptofish", "timestamp": "2025-10-30T22:44:01Z", "comment": "/* top */ Restore previous language, which is NPOV. Treating it as not controversial is POV. \"Words to watch\" are words to be used carefully, not words that must never be used.", "tags": ["wikieditor"], "size": 216076}
