{"rank": 68, "article": "Charlie Kirk", "revid": 1319528570, "parentid": 1319528146, "user": "Mikewem", "timestamp": "2025-10-30T10:28:45Z", "comment": "Undid revision [[Special:Diff/1319518718|1319518718]] by [[Special:Contributions/Wikiediter2029|Wikiediter2029]] ([[User talk:Wikiediter2029|talk]])the neutrality of the article was disputed by an LLM", "tags": ["mw-undo", "mobile edit", "mobile web edit", "advanced mobile edit", "wikieditor"], "size": 216157}
{"rank": 68, "article": "Charlie Kirk", "revid": 1319528146, "parentid": 1319519642, "user": "Mikewem", "timestamp": "2025-10-30T10:23:26Z", "comment": "there is soft support to exclude “controversial” from the lead in [[Wikipedia:Words to avoid in the lead]]. Stronger support is that no form of the word appears in the body. Neither previous version was grammatical, because “promotion” is a verb, not a “view”. I don’t oppose “controversial” in the lead.", "tags": ["mobile edit", "mobile web edit", "advanced mobile edit"], "size": 216273}
